NETWORK ACCESS. fetch() can call HTTPS APIs directly, including APIs without CORS headers: Exhibit relays the request after the user approves the origin and grants relay access. The relay works in the logged-in artifact frame, not in public-link views or top-level exports. Each origin needs the user's approval, and the relay needs one grant per artifact covering every HTTP method; create/write/edit tool results list the origins that will be requested. Fetch the API directly. Never use a public CORS proxy or mode: 'no-cors', and do not build a backend for this. Handle refused approval and request failures in the artifact's interface.
